#: ../../source/etat.rst:4
msgid "Reconstruction de l'état"
msgstr "State reconstruction"

#: ../../source/etat.rst:7
msgid "``Replay`` et ``New``"
msgstr "``Replay`` and ``New``"

#: ../../source/etat.rst:14
msgid "``Replay`` part d'un état neuf :"
msgstr "``Replay`` starts from a new state:"

#: ../../source/etat.rst:20
msgid ""
"puis applique les événements dans l'ordre, chacun passé par "
"``Event.upgraded()`` : un événement de version 0 (libellé en texte) est "
"converti en codes avant d'être appliqué, si bien que le moteur ne voit "
"jamais de libellé texte. À la première erreur, ``Replay`` renvoie l'état "
"partiel **et** une erreur enrichie : ``événement <i> (<kind>) : "
"<erreur>``."
msgstr ""
"then applies the events in order, each passed through "
"``Event.upgraded()``: a version 0 event (label as text) is converted to "
"codes before being applied, so the engine never sees a text label. At the"
" first error, ``Replay`` returns the partial state **and** an enriched "
"error: ``événement <i> (<kind>) : <erreur>``."

#: ../../source/etat.rst:25
msgid ""
"``New`` valide la configuration, construit l'événement ``created`` "
"(``Version: JournalVersion``, soit 2) et l'applique ; elle renvoie "
"l'état, l'événement (que l'hôte doit ajouter en tête de journal) et "
"l'erreur éventuelle."
msgstr ""
"``New`` validates the configuration, builds the ``created`` event "
"(``Version: JournalVersion``, i.e. 2) and applies it; it returns the "
"state, the event (which the host must add at the head of the journal) and"
" the possible error."

#: ../../source/etat.rst:29
msgid ""
"Après chaque événement appliqué, ``Apply`` rafraîchit ``State.Infos`` "
"(``refreshInfos``), incrémente ``NEvents`` et avance ``Last`` si "
"l'horodatage de l'événement est plus récent ; les branches qui sortent "
"tôt (retrait différé) passent par le même chemin (``seen``), pour ne pas "
"fausser le générateur aléatoire, qui dépend de ``NEvents``."
msgstr ""
"After each applied event, ``Apply`` refreshes ``State.Infos`` "
"(``refreshInfos``), increments ``NEvents`` and advances ``Last`` if the "
"event's timestamp is more recent; the branches that exit early (deferred "
"withdrawal) go through the same path (``seen``), so as not to skew the "
"random generator, which depends on ``NEvents``."

#: ../../source/etat.rst:35
msgid "Entrée dans une phase"
msgstr "Entering a phase"

#: ../../source/etat.rst:41
msgid ""
"Ajoute ``p`` à ``ph.Entrants`` (sans doublon) et fixe ``ph.Lives[p] = "
"lives``. Si ``p`` est déjà entrant, **rien n'est modifié** — y compris "
"ses vies."
msgstr ""
"Adds ``p`` to ``ph.Entrants`` (without duplicates) and sets ``ph.Lives[p]"
" = lives``. If ``p`` is already an entrant, **nothing is changed** — "
"including their lives."

#: ../../source/etat.rst:44
msgid ""
"Un inscrit entre dans la première phase à son ``player_added`` si la "
"phase 0 n'est pas tirée et qu'elle est un suisse, ou qu'aucun match n'y "
"est lancé ; il reçoit alors ``livesFor(cfg)``. Un retardataire placé sur "
"une place d'exemption d'un tableau déjà tiré (``player_added`` avec "
"``slot``) prend la place ``BYE`` de la ``Src``, entre avec **une** vie, "
"et ``recompute`` est appelé."
msgstr ""
"A registrant enters the first phase at their ``player_added`` if phase 0 "
"has not been drawn and is a Swiss, or if no match has been started in it;"
" they then receive ``livesFor(cfg)``. A latecomer placed on a bye slot of"
" an already drawn bracket (``player_added`` with ``slot``) takes the "
"``BYE`` place of the ``Src``, enters with **one** life, and ``recompute``"
" is called."

#: ../../source/etat.rst:55
msgid "Kind"
msgstr "Kind"

#: ../../source/etat.rst:55
msgid "Vies à l'entrée"
msgstr "Lives on entry"

#: ../../source/etat.rst:57
msgid "``swiss_lives``"
msgstr "``swiss_lives``"

#: ../../source/etat.rst:57
msgid "``cfg.Lives``"
msgstr "``cfg.Lives``"

#: ../../source/etat.rst:58
msgid "``gsl``"
msgstr "``gsl``"

#: ../../source/etat.rst:58
msgid "2"
msgstr "2"

#: ../../source/etat.rst:59
msgid "tout autre"
msgstr "any other"

#: ../../source/etat.rst:59
msgid "1"
msgstr "1"

#: ../../source/etat.rst:63
msgid "Passage d'une phase à la suivante"
msgstr "Moving from one phase to the next"

#: ../../source/etat.rst:91
msgid ""
"Le cas ``survivors`` est la branche par défaut : toute valeur d'``Entry``"
" autre que ``all`` et ``top:N`` y tombe."
msgstr ""
"The ``survivors`` case is the default branch: any ``Entry`` value other "
"than ``all`` and ``top:N`` falls into it."

#: ../../source/etat.rst:94
msgid ""
"Après des poules, ``survivors(prev)`` = ``rrQualified(prev)`` "
"(``rules.PoolQualified``), **repêchés compris** : un qualifié retiré "
"n'entre pas, et son repêché (s'il y en a un) entre à sa place."
msgstr ""
"After pools, ``survivors(prev)`` = ``rrQualified(prev)`` "
"(``rules.PoolQualified``), **repechaged players included**: a withdrawn "
"qualifier does not enter, and their repechaged player (if any) enters in "
"their place."

#: ../../source/etat.rst:98
msgid ""
"C'est ici que se joue la **bascule à vies** : un joueur qui sort d'un "
"suisse à 2 vies avec ses deux vies intactes entre dans un "
"``lives_bracket`` avec 2 vies, ce qui lui vaudra une **exemption du "
"premier tour**. Un joueur qui n'a plus qu'une vie entre au premier tour."
msgstr ""
"This is where the **switch-over with lives** happens: a player leaving a "
"2-life Swiss with both lives intact enters a ``lives_bracket`` with 2 "
"lives, which earns them a **first-round bye**. A player with only one "
"life left enters in the first round."

#: ../../source/etat.rst:102
#, no-python-format
msgid ""
"``top:N`` est lu par ``Sscanf(\"%d\")`` ; un suffixe illisible donne ``N "
"= 0``, donc une phase vide. Le préfixe est reconnu par ``len(Entry) > 4 "
"&& Entry[:4] == \"top:\"``."
msgstr ""
"``top:N`` is read by ``Sscanf(\"%d\")``; an unreadable suffix gives ``N ="
" 0``, hence an empty phase. The prefix is recognised by ``len(Entry) > 4 "
"&& Entry[:4] == \"top:\"``."

#: ../../source/etat.rst:106
msgid "Vies restantes, joueurs en vie, survivants"
msgstr "Remaining lives, players alive, survivors"

#: ../../source/etat.rst:112
msgid "Enveloppe de ``rules.RemainingLives(lives, losses, withdrawn)`` :"
msgstr "Wrapper of ``rules.RemainingLives(lives, losses, withdrawn)``:"

#: ../../source/etat.rst:123
msgid "Les entrants (dans l'ordre de ``Entrants``) dont ``remainingLives > 0``."
msgstr ""
"The entrants (in the order of ``Entrants``) for whom ``remainingLives > "
"0``."

#: ../../source/etat.rst:130
msgid "Kind de la phase quittée"
msgstr "Kind of the phase being left"

#: ../../source/etat.rst:130
msgid "Survivants"
msgstr "Survivors"

#: ../../source/etat.rst:132
msgid "``round_robin``"
msgstr "``round_robin``"

#: ../../source/etat.rst:132
msgid "``rrQualified(ph)`` — les qualifiés des poules, barrages inclus"
msgstr "``rrQualified(ph)`` — the pool qualifiers, play-offs included"

#: ../../source/etat.rst:135
msgid "``bracket``, ``lives_bracket``"
msgstr "``bracket``, ``lives_bracket``"

#: ../../source/etat.rst:135
msgid ""
"``bracketSurvivors(ph)`` — les entrants si le tableau n'est pas tiré ; le"
" premier du classement si toutes les sections sont finies ; sinon les "
"joueurs de note ``running``"
msgstr ""
"``bracketSurvivors(ph)`` — the entrants if the bracket is not drawn; the "
"first of the standings if all sections are finished; otherwise the "
"players with note ``running``"

#: ../../source/etat.rst:139
msgid "autres (``swiss_lives``, ``gsl``)"
msgstr "others (``swiss_lives``, ``gsl``)"

#: ../../source/etat.rst:139
msgid "``alive(ph)``"
msgstr "``alive(ph)``"

#: ../../source/etat.rst:143
msgid "Comptabilité d'un résultat"
msgstr "Accounting for a result"

#: ../../source/etat.rst:161
msgid ""
"La garde ``ph.Lives[loser] > 0`` évite d'enregistrer comme « éliminé » un"
" joueur qui n'était pas entrant de la phase (cas pathologique après "
"correction)."
msgstr ""
"The guard ``ph.Lives[loser] > 0`` avoids recording as \"eliminated\" a "
"player who was not an entrant of the phase (pathological case after a "
"correction)."

#: ../../source/etat.rst:164
msgid ""
"``ElimOrder`` sert au classement des phases à vies : le **dernier "
"éliminé** quand il ne reste qu'un joueur en vie est le finaliste."
msgstr ""
"``ElimOrder`` serves the standings of the phases with lives: the **last "
"eliminated** when only one player remains alive is the finalist."

#: ../../source/etat.rst:168
msgid "Recalcul complet"
msgstr "Full recomputation"

#: ../../source/etat.rst:174
msgid ""
"Déclenché par ``player_withdrawn`` (immédiat), ``result_corrected``, "
"``match_cancelled``, ``config_changed``, par ``player_added`` sur une "
"place d'exemption (``slot``), et par ``result`` quand un retrait différé "
"prend effet (l'un des deux joueurs du match vient de passer dans "
"``Withdrawn``)."
msgstr ""
"Triggered by ``player_withdrawn`` (immediate), ``result_corrected``, "
"``match_cancelled``, ``config_changed``, by ``player_added`` on a bye "
"slot (``slot``), and by ``result`` when a deferred withdrawal takes "
"effect (one of the two players of the match has just moved to "
"``Withdrawn``)."

#: ../../source/etat.rst:199
msgid ""
"Ce qui **n'est pas** réinitialisé : ``Byes`` et ``ByeRounds`` (un bye "
"reste acquis), ``Entrants``, ``Lives``, ``Round``, ``Roster``, ``Drawn``,"
" ``Repechages`` et ``Sections`` (structure)."
msgstr ""
"What is **not** reset: ``Byes`` and ``ByeRounds`` (a bye remains earned),"
" ``Entrants``, ``Lives``, ``Round``, ``Roster``, ``Drawn``, "
"``Repechages`` and ``Sections`` (structure)."

#: ../../source/etat.rst:203
msgid ""
"``GMatch.MatchID`` repart vide à l'étape 1 et n'est reposé à l'étape 2 "
"que pour les matchs non annulés : une place dont le match vient d'être "
"annulé redevient lançable, au lieu de rester bloquée sur l'identifiant "
"d'un match qui n'existe plus."
msgstr ""
"``GMatch.MatchID`` starts empty again at step 1 and is set again at step "
"2 only for the non-cancelled matches: a slot whose match has just been "
"cancelled becomes startable again, instead of staying blocked on the "
"identifier of a match that no longer exists."

#: ../../source/etat.rst:207
msgid ""
"L'étape 2 fait **deux passes** : relier toutes les places à leur match, "
"puis rejouer les résultats. En une seule passe, ``resolve`` — appelée par"
" ``onResult`` — verrait une place encore sans match dont un joueur est "
"retiré, et la déclarerait gagnée par forfait (``Walkover``) alors que le "
"match a été joué avant le retrait ; le classement ignorerait ce match, et"
" une demi-finaliste retirée finirait dernière."
msgstr ""
"Step 2 makes **two passes**: link all the slots to their match, then "
"replay the results. In a single pass, ``resolve`` — called by "
"``onResult`` — would see a slot still without a match whose player is "
"withdrawn, and would declare it won by forfeit (``Walkover``) although "
"the match was played before the withdrawal; the standings would ignore "
"that match, and a withdrawn semi-finalist would finish last."

#: ../../source/etat.rst:213
msgid ""
"Les **places dérivées** (``GMatch.Players[k]`` dont la source est un "
"autre match) repartent vides à l'étape 1 et sont refaites par ``resolve``"
" : un match qui cesse d'être joué — correction, annulation, ou place "
"d'exemption prise par un retardataire — ne laisse pas derrière lui le "
"joueur qu'il avait fait avancer. Les places **fixes** (``Src[k].Player``,"
" un joueur ou un ``BYE``) sont restaurées telles quelles."
msgstr ""
"The **derived slots** (``GMatch.Players[k]`` whose source is another "
"match) start empty again at step 1 and are rebuilt by ``resolve``: a "
"match that stops being played — correction, cancellation, or bye slot "
"taken by a latecomer — does not leave behind the player it had advanced. "
"The **fixed** slots (``Src[k].Player``, a player or a ``BYE``) are "
"restored as they were."

#: ../../source/etat.rst:220
msgid "Contrôle de cohérence"
msgstr "Consistency check"

#: ../../source/etat.rst:226
msgid ""
"Les avertissements sont des ``Warning`` : un code et ses paramètres, "
"jamais une phrase (le rendu français est ``Warning.String()``, "
"``fr.go``)."
msgstr ""
"The warnings are ``Warning`` values: a code and its parameters, never a "
"sentence (the French rendering is ``Warning.String()``, ``fr.go``)."

#: ../../source/etat.rst:229
#, no-python-brace-format
msgid ""
"Pour chaque match non annulé rattaché à un ``GMatch`` dont les deux "
"places sont connues : si l'ensemble ``{m.A, m.B}`` diffère de "
"``{g.Players[0], g.Players[1]}``, l'avertissement "
"``bracket_wrong_players`` (``Match``, ``Section``, ``Label``, ``A``, "
"``B``, ``ExpectedA`` = ``g.Players[0]``, ``ExpectedB`` = "
"``g.Players[1]``)."
msgstr ""
"For each non-cancelled match attached to a ``GMatch`` whose two slots are"
" known: if the set ``{m.A, m.B}`` differs from ``{g.Players[0], "
"g.Players[1]}``, the warning ``bracket_wrong_players`` (``Match``, "
"``Section``, ``Label``, ``A``, ``B``, ``ExpectedA`` = ``g.Players[0]``, "
"``ExpectedB`` = ``g.Players[1]``)."

#: ../../source/etat.rst:234
msgid ""
"Pour chaque match terminé de longueur ``> 0`` dont un score dépasse la "
"longueur annoncée, l'avertissement ``score_over_length`` (``Match``, "
"``Length``, ``ScoreA``, ``ScoreB``)."
msgstr ""
"For each finished match of length ``> 0`` where a score exceeds the "
"announced length, the warning ``score_over_length`` (``Match``, "
"``Length``, ``ScoreA``, ``ScoreB``)."

#: ../../source/etat.rst:237
msgid ""
"Dans les phases ``swiss_lives``, deux avertissements disent ce qu'une "
"correction (ou une annulation) a changé à la vie d'un joueur — un suisse "
"n'a pas de graphe, donc pas de ``bracket_wrong_players`` :"
msgstr ""
"In the ``swiss_lives`` phases, two warnings say what a correction (or a "
"cancellation) changed in a player's life — a Swiss has no graph, hence no"
" ``bracket_wrong_players``:"

#: ../../source/etat.rst:240
msgid ""
"``correction_eliminates_running`` (``Match``, ``Player``, ``A``, ``B``, "
"``Label``) : un match **en cours** dont un joueur n'a plus aucune vie. "
"Cela n'arrive pas dans un tournoi mené normalement — on ne lance pas un "
"joueur éliminé — ; c'est la trace d'une correction d'un résultat "
"antérieur qui l'a éliminé pendant qu'il jouait (un joueur retiré n'est "
"pas signalé). L'annulation du match est proposée (``cancel_match``, "
"``reparation.go`` ; voir :ref:`propositions`). L'avertissement tombe "
"quand le match finit ou est annulé."
msgstr ""
"``correction_eliminates_running`` (``Match``, ``Player``, ``A``, ``B``, "
"``Label``): a match **in progress** in which a player has no life left. "
"This does not happen in a normally run tournament — an eliminated player "
"is not started — ; it is the trace of a correction to an earlier result "
"that eliminated them while they were playing (a withdrawn player is not "
"flagged). Cancelling the match is proposed (``cancel_match``, "
"``reparation.go``; see :ref:`propositions`). The warning goes away when "
"the match finishes or is cancelled."

#: ../../source/etat.rst:246
msgid ""
"``correction_revives`` (``Player``) : un joueur que la correction a rendu"
" à la vie (``State.Revived``). Il est de nouveau appariable, et le moteur"
" le dit jusqu'à ce qu'il rejoue — ou qu'une autre correction l'élimine de"
" nouveau. ``Revived`` est tenu par ``noteRevived``, qui compare les "
"joueurs en vie dans les phases suisses avant et après "
"``result_corrected`` ou ``match_cancelled`` ; un ``match_started`` en "
"retire ses deux joueurs. Les avertissements sont émis dans l'ordre des "
"identifiants (``sortedIDs``)."
msgstr ""
"``correction_revives`` (``Player``): a player whom the correction brought"
" back to life (``State.Revived``). They can be paired again, and the "
"engine says so until they play again — or another correction eliminates "
"them again. ``Revived`` is maintained by ``noteRevived``, which compares "
"the players alive in the Swiss phases before and after "
"``result_corrected`` or ``match_cancelled``; a ``match_started`` removes "
"its two players from it. The warnings are emitted in identifier order "
"(``sortedIDs``)."

#: ../../source/etat.rst:253
msgid ""
"Et pour chaque table qui porte **plusieurs matchs en cours**, "
"l'avertissement ``table_shared``, une fois par match arrivé en second "
"dans ``MatchOrder``, avec ``Table``, ``Match`` (ce match), ``A``, ``B`` "
"et ``Other`` (le premier occupant). Il est dérivé de l'état : il "
"disparaît quand l'un des deux matchs se termine, est annulé ou change de "
"table. Un match sans table (``Table = 0``) ne partage rien. Le score est "
"**enregistré** malgré tout : pendant un tournoi, c'est la parole du TD "
"qui fait foi ; le moteur le signale, il ne le refuse pas."
msgstr ""
"And for each table carrying **several matches in progress**, the warning "
"``table_shared``, once per match that arrived second in ``MatchOrder``, "
"with ``Table``, ``Match`` (this match), ``A``, ``B`` and ``Other`` (the "
"first occupant). It is derived from the state: it disappears when one of "
"the two matches finishes, is cancelled or changes table. A match without "
"a table (``Table = 0``) shares nothing. The score is **recorded** anyway:"
" during a tournament, the TD's word is authoritative; the engine flags "
"it, it does not refuse it."

#: ../../source/etat.rst:260
msgid ""
"``check`` est rappelée après **tout événement qui touche un match** : "
"``result``, ``match_started`` et ``table_changed`` directement, les "
"autres (``result_corrected``, ``match_cancelled``, ``player_withdrawn``, "
"``config_changed``) par ``recompute``, qui la termine (puis de nouveau "
"par ``noteRevived`` après une correction ou une annulation). Un "
"avertissement qui n'apparaîtrait qu'après une correction sans rapport ne "
"servirait à rien : le TD doit le voir au moment où il peut encore agir. "
"``length_changed`` ne touche que les matchs FUTURS d'une phase et ne "
"change donc rien à ce que ``check`` regarde."
msgstr ""
"``check`` is called again after **any event that touches a match**: "
"``result``, ``match_started`` and ``table_changed`` directly, the others "
"(``result_corrected``, ``match_cancelled``, ``player_withdrawn``, "
"``config_changed``) through ``recompute``, which ends with it (then again"
" through ``noteRevived`` after a correction or a cancellation). A warning"
" that appeared only after an unrelated correction would be useless: the "
"TD must see it at the moment they can still act. ``length_changed`` "
"touches only the FUTURE matches of a phase and so changes nothing of what"
" ``check`` looks at."

#: ../../source/etat.rst:268
msgid ""
"Elle parcourt les **graphes** et non les matchs — chaque place connaît "
"son match par ``MatchID`` — parce que chercher, pour chaque match, sa "
"place dans toutes les sections serait quadratique, et ``check`` tourne à "
"chaque résultat. L'ordre des avertissements est : pour chaque match dans "
"l'ordre de ``MatchOrder`` (celui que le TD lit), "
"``bracket_wrong_players`` puis ``score_over_length`` ; ensuite "
"``correction_eliminates_running`` et ``correction_revives`` ; enfin "
"``table_shared``."
msgstr ""
"It walks the **graphs** and not the matches — each slot knows its match "
"through ``MatchID`` — because looking up, for each match, its slot in all"
" the sections would be quadratic, and ``check`` runs at every result. The"
" order of the warnings is: for each match in the order of ``MatchOrder`` "
"(the one the TD reads), ``bracket_wrong_players`` then "
"``score_over_length``; then ``correction_eliminates_running`` and "
"``correction_revives``; finally ``table_shared``."

#: ../../source/etat.rst:274
msgid ""
"``State.Warnings`` **doit être vide** dans un tournoi mené normalement ; "
"c'est un invariant vérifié par les tests. Sa non-vacuité signale au TD "
"qu'une correction a désynchronisé un tableau, ou qu'un score est "
"incohérent."
msgstr ""
"``State.Warnings`` **must be empty** in a normally run tournament; this "
"is an invariant checked by the tests. If it is non-empty, it tells the TD"
" that a correction has desynchronised a bracket, or that a score is "
"inconsistent."
